**Top k frequent words with tie-breaking.** Given `words` and `k`, return the `k` most frequent words, ordered from highest frequency to lowest; words with the **same frequency** must be ordered alphabetically (smaller string first). You may assume `k <=` the number of distinct words. Use an `unordered_map` for counts and a **size-k heap with a custom comparator** (do not sort all distinct words).

```cpp
